   "text": {
    "L1": "To get to school safely, cross only at a zebra crossing, foot overbridge or subway, or with a signal or traffic police person.",
    "L2": "A parked bus can hide you from a driver, and it can hide the vehicle from you. Never cross from behind or in front of it.",
    "L3": "First, stop at the edge of the crossing and listen. If there is a signal, wait for the green walking figure.",
    "L4": "In India, vehicles drive on the left, so the nearest traffic comes from your right. Look right, then left, then right again.",
    "L5": "When the way is clear, walk briskly in a straight line and keep looking. Never run or zig-zag across the road.",
    "L6": "Use the footpath after crossing. If there is no footpath, walk on the right edge facing traffic coming towards you.",
    "L7": "On a school bus, wait until it stops fully, keep your hands and head inside, and wear a seat belt if there is one.",
    "L8": "Now put the three looks in the correct order."
   },
